{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And Elohim tested Abraham.</b> Some say the samekh is in place of shin, and the heh in place of alef, but the sense of the entire passage refutes them; rather, נסה is according to its plain meaning. And the people of speculative reasoning said that knowledge is of two kinds: one is knowledge of the future before it comes to be, and the second is knowledge of the existent thing now present — and this is the meaning of נסה, as in 'now I know.' And the Gaon [Saadia] said that the word נסה is to show his righteousness to human beings, and the word ידעתי is in the sense of הודעתי, 'I made known' — but does this Gaon not know that at the time he bound his son, not even his young men were there? And others said that the meaning of 'and offer him there as a burnt offering' is that he should bring him up to the mountain, and this would be counted for him as a burnt offering, and Abraham did not know the secret of the prophecy, and he hastened to slaughter him, and HaShem said to him, 'I did not request this.' And others said: he showed him that he would bring him up as a burnt offering, like 'and give them wine to drink' (Jeremiah 35:2). And these Geonim needed to interpret the word האלה, for they say it is impossible that after HaShem commands a commandment he would then say, 'Do not do it.' But did they not set their mind on the firstborn, whom he exchanged for Levites after a year? And after the verse says at the outset, 'And Elohim tested Abraham,' all the arguments fall away — and HaShem tested him so that he would receive reward." "And the meaning of 'for now I know' is like 'that I may know' (Genesis 18:21). And further I will explain its secret in the verse 'I have known you by name' (Exodus 33:12), if HaShem who knows hidden things helps me."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {0 "Resolved הגאונים as 'the Geonim' (plural), referring to the rabbinic authorities cited collectively in the preceding dispute."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:45:27.283251082Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}